To turn this mock-up into a colorful website, you can create a basic HTML structure and add CSS styles to make the website visually appealing. Here's a simple example of how to create a website with the two jokes displayed:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>My Joke Website</title>
  <style>
    /* Add some basic styles for the website */
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f5f5f5;
    }

    h1 {
      color: #333;
    }

    p {
      color: #666;
    }

    .joke {
      font-size: 24px;
      margin: 20px 0;
      padding: 20px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      background-color: #fff;
      box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
    }

    .joke:nth-child(even) {
      background-color: #f5f5f5;
    }

    .joke:nth-child(odd) {
      background-color: #ddd;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
  <div class="joke">
    <p>I once heard a joke that was so funny, I laughed for hours!</p>
    <p>I'm not sure if it was the joke itself or the fact that I was sitting in a chair that made me laugh so much.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="joke">
    <p>I'm not a comedian, but I do have a joke that I find pretty funny:</p>
    <p>Why was the math book sad? Because it had too many problems.</p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```
